<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Dole</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1877–1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as James Drummond Dole</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dole">Dole</a> was an American businessman who founded the Hawaiian Pineapple Company in 1901 and became known as the 'Pineapple King'. He planted pineapples on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oahu</a>, bought the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lanai">Lanai</a> in 1922 to turn it into a vast plantation, and promoted canned pineapple across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. His company was a forerunner of the Dole Food Company.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-dole.jpg" alt="James Dole" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: From Bain News service collection; writing in lower right looks like &quot;Hartsook&quot; · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Drummond_Dole.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
